node_modules/
.turbo/
.eslintcache
# dist/ everywhere except ts/packages/core, whose build output is committed deliberately (see that package's README): consumers install it as a git-subdirectory dependency (github:ExaDev/wire-mesh#path:ts/packages/core), and a git install always resolves under node_modules where no build step can run -- the same reasoning as ExaDev/cddl.js committing its own dist. CI rebuilds and diffs, so it cannot drift from src/.
dist/
!ts/packages/core/dist/
!ts/packages/core/dist/**
